{"agent_id":"pp3g-JQ9d-fix-missing-opencode-ai-tui-logo-run-bun-install-in","agent_seq":14,"timestamp":"2026-09-02T04:03:04.611303307Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b1dfdeb3-a85a-402c-b912-8b26718693f5","comment_uuid":"21e51aa5-a6a2-4995-be2a-5733f119ebe7","author":"pp3g-JQ9d-fix-missing-opencode-ai-tui-logo-run-bun-install-in","content":"Result: Fix dialog Yes logged as cancelled — text click bubbling (issue #510, branch feature/stop-button, commit 6aa967a2).\n\nWHAT: Fix in fork/opencode-src/packages/tui/src/component/prompt/index.tsx:265-290 — outer box onMouseUp did not bubble from inner <text>Yes/No</text> in opentui, so clicking the text hit the <text> not the <box> and resolved via dialog onClose fallback false (Yes→cancelled). Added onMouseUp handlers to inner <text>Yes</text> and <text>No</text> duplicating the outer box handlers so both padding and text clicks resolve correctly (Yes→true→1 interrupt, No→false→0). Add discriminating log confirmed=${confirmed} before dialogEvent mapping in stop-button-controller.ts:206 to make the mis-route visible (Yes mis-as-cancelled would show confirmed=false vs true). Add 3 integration tests in stop-button-controller.test.ts simulating text clicks: Yes text→1 interrupt + confirmed=true, No text→0 + confirmed=false + cancelled, discriminating log test that Yes and No logs differ.\n\nWHY: Placebo-worse-than-no-button — user clicked Yes on text and the agent kept running with a cancelled log, indistinguishable from a real No without the confirmed log. Cheapest discriminating test is the confirmed log + text-click interrupt count.\n\nHOW CERTAIN: evidence-based. Re-ran: bun test tui 275 pass/1 skip (49 files, 7895 expects) — incl. machine 44 pass/723 expects (stop-button-machine.test.ts) and controller 21 pass/60 expects (was 18, +3 new text-click tests); core 1107 pass (incl. coordinator 18/30 + identity 24/67 =42); core tsgo --noEmit clean; tui tsgo --noEmit shows only pre-existing unrelated errors in stop-button-proptest/xstate fast-check files, no new errors in stop-button files; probe bash -n OK; mutation: removing inner text handlers would still pass outer-box clicks but the new text-click tests would fail (Yes→0); removing confirmed log would fail the discriminating log test.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: Interactive TUI mouse QA (manual click on Yes text in live opentui); live 9-point probe on tool-child-capable server (SKIP when down, covered at coordinator seam); cargo test N/A (no Cargo.toml in fork, bun tests are the carrier).","created_at":"2026-09-02T04:03:04.605486558Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:ABole7xErsKGlHRjxbmSnjnDlFg7BP+04GRft7gAl04","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgTLOSXNCSri4cFaVZ01fDunyK95xEEl0pnFilOVSprDYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAkwjJF7+gbGavwE41NfNXYmenedXJmaUZ+XIelEXnUm+6lk+DfYxbkVJmPy9vFptOKxtYNWcEmffjNt+tKEzcBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:ABole7xErsKGlHRjxbmSnjnDlFg7BP+04GRft7gAl04","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgTLOSXNCSri4cFaVZ01fDunyK95xEEl0pnFilOVSprDYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD8AFTgAc95eumaOC5FJQXlTAWh15joRp91nwi85BUO9gXBz8Ht0cu5UPpC1Qv2nB0zAxTO3uZasISzPjCCx7g8="}
